Thanks for the report. Could you confirm whether this still occurs on the latest VS Code build and provide:

- the chat mode, selected model, prompt, and exact steps that leave the request pending;
- whether Chat responds in a local window on the same machine;
- the Chat, GitHub Copilot, and Remote SSH output logs captured during one failed request; and
- whether the SSH/VNC connection also disconnects when Chat is not being used?

This issue will automatically close after 7 days if the requested information is not provided.

Thanks for the report. To identify whether this comes from editor restoration, Copilot, or Remote-SSH, could you confirm it on the latest VS Code build and provide:

- results with Copilot disabled, and separately in a local window with the same files restored;
- the busy process shown by **Developer: Open Process Explorer** while the window is unresponsive;
- a performance profile captured using https://github.com/microsoft/vscode/wiki/Performance-Issues;
- the approximate number of restored editors and whether closing them before reopening the workspace avoids the freeze.

The `info-needed` label will automatically close this issue after 7 days without a reply.

Thanks for the report. To investigate, please provide:

- which chat surface/provider owns the blank conversations (for example, GitHub Copilot Chat, Claude Code, Gemini, or ChatGPT);
- exact steps from creating a conversation through reopening it, including whether the workspace is local or connected through Remote-SSH;
- whether the issue remains with unrelated third-party chat extensions disabled; and
- the relevant ChatSessionStore, window, and chat-provider log entries produced when you click a blank conversation.

Issues labeled `info-needed` automatically close after 7 days without a reply.

Thanks for the report. To identify which undo stack deleted the file, could you please provide:

- the exact steps immediately before pressing Ctrl+Z, including how the file was created and whether Chat, Copilot CLI, or another extension changed it;
- which editor, view, or terminal had focus when Ctrl+Z was pressed;
- whether this reproduces on the latest VS Code build with extensions disabled; and
- whether the deleted file appears in the Recycle Bin or the Timeline/Local History view.

If possible, please include a minimal sample workspace or screen recording. This issue will automatically close after 7 days without the requested information.
